 "conclusions": [
  "cuFINUFFT-style shared-memory subproblems and privatized shared grids are slower than global FP64 atomics on the RTX 5080 (FP64 shared atomics no cheaper).",
  "One thread per fine point (exact-pair gather) is occupancy- and imbalance-bound: up to 2.9e4 copies per point.",
  "Spread time is spread over many mid-size rectangles (512-4096 modes ~2/3), not a few dense ones; raising the NUFFT mode floor to 64-512 changes nothing.",
  "Balanced warp gather over sorted, batched copies cuts the spread phase 4-6x; fused key/modulation kernels keep most of it at flush level."
